he Senate will now consider the proposal from Senator Hanson, submitted under standing order 75 today, which has also been circulated and is shown on the Dynamic Red: That in the opinion of the Senate, the following is a matter of urgency: The need for the Albanese Labor government to abandon its migration policies that will add an extra 1 million people to Australia's population over the next four years on top of the 1.6 million people Labor has already added since coming to office. Is consideration of the proposal supported? _More than the number of senators required by the standing orders having risen in their places—_ With the concurrence of the Senate, the clerks will set the clock in line with the informal arrangements made by the whips. Pauline Hanson I move: That in the opinion of the Senate, the following is a matter of urgency: The need for the Albanese Labor government to abandon its migration policies that will add an extra 1 million people to Australia's population over the next four years on top of the 1.6 million people Labor has already added since coming to office. I'll tell the Australian people why the government are doing this. The government is using mass migration to prop up the GDP and to cover up their economic mismanagement. Now the Australian people have a choice. One Nation will cut the number of temporary visa holders in the country by more than 750,000 over a period of three years. Labor intend to add an extra million. Some people aren't reading One Nation's policies. Why? It's because they choose to ridicule us just because we're One Nation. We aren't cutting backpackers, WHMs. We're not cutting the PALM scheme. We aren't cutting any skilled temporary migrants. One Nation will cut the number of temporary visa holders to 2017 levels. The economy didn't crash in 2017, and, in fact, many Australians were better off. We will also restore the number of temporary international students to 2015 levels, a time when our universitie","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10803","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-09-16/15"}
